17. Current One-Minute Project Explanation

KubeMentor is a Kubernetes learning platform I am building from scratch as a long-term DevOps portfolio project. I started with a Python Flask application and created root, health, and readiness endpoints. I introduced automated testing with pytest and deliberately tested failure scenarios so I could understand how CI will detect broken changes. During the initial build I also troubleshot Linux process management when a suspended Flask process kept port 5000 occupied, and I diagnosed a Python import-path problem when pytest could not load the application package. The project will progressively move through PostgreSQL, authentication, Docker Compose, CI quality gates, Kubernetes, persistent storage, Vault, External Secrets, Reloader, Helm, Argo CD, GitOps, multi-environment deployment, security, and PWA/mobile capabilities.

